<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Android 12+ (API 31+) backup and device-transfer rules. Nothing leaves the
  device. `android:allowBackup="false"` covers cloud backup on every API level;
  from 31 the device-to-device transfer channel is governed here instead, so
  both are stated explicitly rather than left to a default.

  What this protects: the Hive box `detoxo` holds the manually protected app
  list (the inventory of someone's banking / UPI / password apps) and, since the
  onboarding step machine, their first name, self-reported screen-time band and
  the social feeds they use. `detoxo_engine_prefs` mirrors the protected
  packages natively. `docs/code_docs/24-protected-apps.md` §6 promises the
  protected list "never leaves the device"; the platform default
  (`allowBackup=true`) made that claim false.

  Why everything rather than a path list: Detoxo is offline-first with no
  account, so a restore carries nothing the user would miss beyond local
  settings — and an exclusion keyed to a Hive file path would fail silently and
  invisibly if path_provider's directory ever moved. Excluding wholesale is the
  version that cannot quietly stop working.

  Accepted cost: after a restore or a device transfer the user re-does
  onboarding and re-adds any manual protections. Catalog-derived protection is
  computed, not stored, so it is unaffected.
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup>
        <exclude domain="root" path="." />
    </cloud-backup>
    <device-transfer>
        <exclude domain="root" path="." />
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
